   "unmapped": [
    "Contamination is a set of (round, arm) locations chosen before the game. The adversary assigns arbitrary losses there. The contamination is 'moderate after tau rounds': for all t >= tau, the number of contaminated locations of each suboptimal arm up to t is at most t*Delta(a)/4, and of each best arm at most t*Delta/4. The limit is on the number of contaminated locations, not on a total corruption budget C."
   ],
   "definition_quote": "Contaminated stochastic regime. In this regime the adversary picks some round-arm pairs (t, a) (\"locations\") before the game starts and assigns the loss values there in an arbitrary way. The remaining losses are generated according to the stochastic regime. We call a contaminated stochastic regime moderately contaminated after tau rounds if for all t >= tau the total number of contaminated locations of each suboptimal arm up to time t is at most tDelta(a)/4 and the number of contaminated locations of each best arm is at most tDelta/4."
  },
